# DnD And DropZone Contracts

When adding or changing drag/drop behavior in the frontend, keep DnD contracts explicit and centralized.

- Define drag/drop string constants, shared data shapes, and type guards in `src/features/core/dnd/`; do not scatter raw `dropType` / drag `type` strings across components.
- Use the current drop responsibilities:
  - `canvas`: editor canvas target. Sidebar node templates create nodes; sidebar graph resources open graph tabs.
  - `graph-folder`: sidebar Event/Function folder target. Moving here must update the project file location through backend commands.
  - `tabbar`: tab reorder/move target.
  - `layout-region`: editor layout docking/splitting target.
- Do not add another overlapping full-editor DropZone for opening graphs. Reuse `CanvasDropZone` for graph-open behavior and visual feedback.
- `Workspace` should orchestrate drag end routing; visual drop zones should only expose typed drop data and lightweight hover UI.
- Sidebar graph resources must carry `{ id, name, type, folderPath }` so drops can either open the graph or move its file-backed folder.

```typescript
// Good
data: { dropType: DROP_TYPES.CANVAS, groupId }
if (isCanvasDrop(overData)) { /* route canvas drop */ }

// Bad
data: { dropType: "canvas", groupId }
if (overData?.dropType === "canvas") { /* scattered string */ }
```
